module imagingODDetection
module waveletODSorting
module sixteenSrRNASequencing
module antibioticResistanceDetection

manifest FecalCellSuspension
manifest BHIS_Medium
manifest GMM_Medium
manifest YCFA_Medium
manifest HFE7500_SurfactantOil
manifest Ampicillin_BHIS
manifest Ciprofloxacin_BHIS
manifest Vancomycin_BHIS
manifest DNAExtractionBuffer
manifest PFO_DemulsificationAgent

// ============================================================
// Droplet-Based High-Throughput Cultivation for Accurate
// Screening of Antibiotic Resistant Gut Microbes.
// Watterson et al., eLife 2020;9:e56998.
// DOI: https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.56998
//
// Platform: Anaerobic vinyl chamber (Coy Laboratory Products),
// 86% N2 / 10% CO2 / 4% H2 atmosphere, <1 ppm O2. All droplet
// generation, cultivation, and sorting steps are performed
// inside the anaerobic chamber. External computer controls
// syringe pumps, high-frame-rate camera (Basler acA640-750um,
// 925 Hz, 59 us exposure), and sorting electrodes (10 kHz,
// 800 V p-p, 30% duty cycle, 10 ms actuation).
//
// DROPLET GENERATION: Flow-focusing junction. Oil phase:
// Bio-Rad Droplet Generation Oil for EvaGreen. Droplet volumes:
// ~65-115 pL. Fecal cell suspension diluted 200x so that
// ~2-12% of droplets contain exactly one viable cell
// (Poisson statistics). ~4-15 million droplets per run.
//
// SORTING: Wavelet OD image analysis (discrete wavelet frame
// decomposition, biorthogonal 3.1 wavelets, LL High subband,
// 15x15 px window, 5 px step, 15 grey levels, 3x3 px
// displacement). Wavelet OD in [0.3, 0.7] = sparse/slow-growing
// colony (KEEP). OD < 0.3 = empty. OD > 0.7 = dense colony.
// Sorting rate: ~30 Hz. Dielectrophoretic deflection into
// keep/waste path.
//
// SEQUENCING: Paired-end 16S rRNA V4 amplicon sequencing
// (Illumina MiSeq, 2x151). Library prep by Argonne National
// Laboratory Earth Microbiome Project protocol. ASVs inferred
// by Minimum Entropy Decomposition (MED); taxonomy by SILVA.
//
// BIOLOGICAL SCOPE: This file encodes the full experiment
// in sequence:
//   PROTOCOL 1 - Rich media droplet cultivation (BHIS, GMM,
//     YCFA), with slow-grower sorting enrichment.
//   PROTOCOL 2 - Antibiotic resistance screening in droplets
//     (Ampicillin, Ciprofloxacin, Vancomycin in BHIS).
// Each protocol block is self-contained with its own QC gate.
//
// NOTE ON INCUBATION TIME: BioScript duration tokens are
// s / m only. All hour-based incubations are converted to
// minutes. Plates: up to 7 days = 10080 min. Droplets:
// up to 2 days = 2880 min.
//
// NOTE ON DISPENSE ABSTRACTION: `dispense 1 units of X`
// models the generation of one droplet batch (~0.5-1 mL
// emulsion) from a given medium/reagent reservoir. Each
// dispense into oil at the flow-focusing junction produces
// the full set of encapsulated droplets for that condition.
// The oil phase (HFE7500_SurfactantOil) is modelled as a
// co-dispense step via `mix`, abstracting the two-pump
// (aqueous + oil) flow-focusing generation event.
//
// NOTE ON POISSON ENCAPSULATION: Stochastic single-cell
// isolation by Poisson statistics is implicit in the
// dispense step. There is no reagent-mixing in the DMF
// sense; `mix` abstracts a droplet generation/coalescence
// event at the flow-focusing junction.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- device setup; BHIS rich media
//                              droplet cultivation
//   BB2  bhisDropletPass    -- bhisCultSignal > 0: growth
//                              detected; proceed to sorting
//   BB3  bhisDropletFail    -- bhisCultSignal <= 0: no growth;
//                              drain emulsion
//   BB4  bhisCultJoin       -- join: slow-grower sorting
//   BB5  bhisSortPass       -- bioxSortSignal > 0: slow-grower
//                              colonies kept; proceed to seq
//   BB6  bhisSortFail       -- bioxSortSignal <= 0: sort failed;
//                              drain sorted fraction
//   BB7  bhisSortJoin       -- join: GMM cultivation arm
//   BB8  gmmDropletPass     -- gmmCultSignal > 0: growth; proceed
//   BB9  gmmDropletFail     -- gmmCultSignal <= 0: no growth; drain
//   BB10 gmmCultJoin        -- join: YCFA cultivation arm
//   BB11 ycfaDropletPass    -- ycfaCultSignal > 0: growth; proceed
//   BB12 ycfaDropletFail    -- ycfaCultSignal <= 0: no growth; drain
//   BB13 ycfaCultJoin       -- join: antibiotic screening arm
//   BB14 ampDropletPass     -- ampResistSignal > 0: resistant
//                              organisms detected; proceed
//   BB15 ampDropletFail     -- ampResistSignal <= 0: none; drain
//   BB16 ampScreenJoin      -- join: ciprofloxacin arm
//   BB17 ciproDropletPass   -- ciproResistSignal > 0: proceed
//   BB18 ciproDropletFail   -- ciproResistSignal <= 0: drain
//   BB19 ciproScreenJoin    -- join: vancomycin arm
//   BB20 vancoDropletPass   -- vancoResistSignal > 0: proceed
//   BB21 vancoDropletFail   -- vancoResistSignal <= 0: drain
//   BB22 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 1: RICH MEDIA DROPLET CULTIVATION
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 1: Prepare BHIS emulsion.
//   Fecal cell suspension (FMT donor, previously characterised
//   by Lee et al. 2017) diluted 200x into Brain Heart Infusion
//   Supplemented medium (BHIS: 18.5 g BHI broth, 2.5 g yeast
//   extract, 0.25 g L-cysteine per 500 mL; autoclaved; + 0.5 mL
//   0.1% Vitamin K + 0.5 mL hemin 5 mg/mL).
//   Live cell density: ~1.5 +/- 1.0 x10^8 cells/mL.
//   Poisson loading: ~2-12% of droplets contain one live cell.
//   Droplet generation flow-focusing junction; HFE7500 oil
//   phase abstracts the two-pump co-dispense event.
//   Total emulsion: ~0.5-1 mL of 65-115 pL droplets
//   (~4-15 million droplets).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisCells      = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
bhisMedium     = dispense 1 units of BHIS_Medium
bhisOil        = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

// Mix abstracts the flow-focusing droplet generation event:
// aqueous (cells + medium) sheared into oil at junction.
bhisPreEmulsion  = mix bhisCells with bhisMedium for 5s
bhisEmulsion     = mix bhisPreEmulsion with bhisOil for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 2: Incubate BHIS droplets.
//   Emulsion stored in 15 mL snap-cap culture tube at 37 C
//   inside the anaerobic chamber incubator. Cultured up to
//   2 days (2880 min). Each isolated droplet acts as an
//   independent microreactor; slow-growers avoid competitive
//   overgrowth from fast-growing populations.
//   NOTE: Droplet volume reduction begins after ~4 days due
//   to evaporation in the arid anaerobic atmosphere; cultures
//   are limited to 2 days to avoid this artefact.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat bhisEmulsion at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 3: Image-based colony density detection.
//   High-frame-rate camera + LabView code detects each droplet
//   approaching the sorting junction. Wavelet OD computed per
//   droplet. This detect step abstracts the imaging pass to
//   assess whether colonies have grown in the emulsion before
//   sorting. A positive signal (> 0) indicates colonies
//   present in the emulsion at detectable density.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisCultSignal = detect imagingODDetection on bhisEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: BHIS cultivation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): bhisCultSignal > 0 -> colony-containing droplets
//             detected; carry emulsion forward to sorting.
// Fail (BB3): bhisCultSignal <= 0 -> no growth detected;
//             drain emulsion (all droplets empty).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (bhisCultJoin).
// ============================================================

if (bhisCultSignal > 0) {
    dispose bhisCultSignal
} else {
    drain bhisEmulsion
    dispose bhisCultSignal
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: bhisCultJoin
// Control falls into the slow-grower sorting arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 4: Slow-grower sorting in BHIS droplets.
//   Two independent sorting experiments (biological replicates).
//   Droplets re-injected at 20 uL/hr; oil spacing phase at
//   180 uL/hr. Camera detects each droplet; Wavelet OD computed.
//   Droplets with Wavelet OD in [0.3, 0.7] (sparse colony)
//   are deflected to the keep path via 10 kHz, 800 V p-p
//   electrode actuation for 10 ms. Dense colonies (OD > 0.7)
//   and empty droplets (OD < 0.3) pass to waste.
//   Sorting rate: ~30 Hz. False positive rate: <= 8%.
//   Sorted volume much less than 100 uL (limited by ~30 Hz rate);
//   sorted layer is ~1-10 uL on top of oil.
//   Result: shift in rank-abundance curve; average amplified
//   ASVs from <1% to >1%: 6.5 (unsorted) vs 12.5 (sorted)
//   out of 158 total ASVs detected.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bioxSortSignal = detect waveletODSorting on bhisEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: BHIS slow-grower sort QC gate
// Pass (BB5): bioxSortSignal > 0 -> slow-grower colonies
//             successfully isolated in keep path; proceed
//             to sequencing.
// Fail (BB6): bioxSortSignal <= 0 -> sort failed (no sparse
//             colonies present); drain sorted fraction.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (bhisSortJoin).
// ============================================================

if (bioxSortSignal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // Recovery and sequencing (pass path only):
    // Sorted droplets (~1-10 uL) mixed with equal volume of
    // 1H,1H,2H,2H-Perfluoro-1-octanol (PFO) for demulsification.
    // Vortex + centrifuge; oil and PFO removed. For sorted
    // volumes, add 150 uL DNA-free water + 150 uL PFO first.
    // DNA extracted using Qiagen DNeasy Blood and Tissue Kit.
    // Paired-end 16S rRNA V4 amplicon sequencing (Illumina
    // MiSeq 2x151); ASVs by MED; taxonomy by SILVA.
    // Separately: streaked sorted droplets onto BHIS agar,
    // cultured 2 days at 37 C; 24 random colonies picked for
    // Sanger sequencing (16S, 27F/1492R primers).
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    pfo1             = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer1       = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedBHIS  = mix bhisEmulsion with pfo1 for 1m
    extractedDNA_BHIS = mix demulsifiedBHIS with dnaBuffer1 for 1m

    bhisSeqSignal    = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_BHIS for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_BHIS
    dispose bhisSeqSignal
} else {
    drain bhisEmulsion
}

dispose bioxSortSignal

// ============================================================
// BB7: bhisSortJoin
// BHIS arm complete. Control falls into GMM cultivation arm.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 5: Prepare and incubate GMM emulsion.
//   Gut Microbiota Medium (GMM), prepared per Goodman et al.
//   2011. Same fecal cell suspension, same Poisson loading
//   (200x dilution), same droplet volume range (65-115 pL).
//   Parallel plate cultures also prepared for comparison
//   (up to 7 days, 10080 min on plates vs 2880 min in droplets).
//   Droplets show 16S-based richness increase relative to
//   plate cultures across all media (p<0.005, Mann-Whitney U).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gmmCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
gmmMedium    = dispense 1 units of GMM_Medium
gmmOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

gmmPreEmulsion  = mix gmmCells with gmmMedium for 5s
gmmEmulsion     = mix gmmPreEmulsion with gmmOil for 5s

heat gmmEmulsion at 37c for 2880m

gmmCultSignal   = detect imagingODDetection on gmmEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: GMM cultivation QC gate
// Pass (BB8): gmmCultSignal > 0 -> growth detected; extract
//             DNA and sequence.
// Fail (BB9): gmmCultSignal <= 0 -> no growth; drain.
// Both converge at BB10 (gmmCultJoin).
// ============================================================

if (gmmCultSignal > 0) {
    pfo2              = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer2        = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedGMM    = mix gmmEmulsion with pfo2 for 1m
    extractedDNA_GMM  = mix demulsifiedGMM with dnaBuffer2 for 1m

    gmmSeqSignal      = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_GMM for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_GMM
    dispose gmmSeqSignal
} else {
    drain gmmEmulsion
}

dispose gmmCultSignal

// ============================================================
// BB10: gmmCultJoin
// GMM arm complete. Control falls into YCFA cultivation arm.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 6: Prepare and incubate YCFA emulsion.
//   Yeast Casitones Fatty Acid medium (YCFA), modified DSMZ
//   media 1611: 10 g casitone, 2.5 g yeast extract, 5 g
//   dextrose, MgSO4, CaCl2, KH2PO4, K2HPO4, NaCl, resazurin,
//   volatile fatty acids (acetic, propionic, iso-butyric,
//   n-valeric, iso-valeric); pH 6.7-6.8 + vitamin solution
//   post-autoclaving.
//   YCFA showed the largest richness increase (up to 410%)
//   over plate cultures (p<0.005, Mann-Whitney U test).
//   Notable lack of Bacteroidetes on YCFA plates (competitive
//   exclusion) was abolished in droplets (phyla-broad growth).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ycfaCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
ycfaMedium    = dispense 1 units of YCFA_Medium
ycfaOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

ycfaPreEmulsion  = mix ycfaCells with ycfaMedium for 5s
ycfaEmulsion     = mix ycfaPreEmulsion with ycfaOil for 5s

heat ycfaEmulsion at 37c for 2880m

ycfaCultSignal   = detect imagingODDetection on ycfaEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: YCFA cultivation QC gate
// Pass (BB11): ycfaCultSignal > 0 -> growth detected; extract
//              DNA and sequence.
// Fail (BB12): ycfaCultSignal <= 0 -> no growth; drain.
// Both converge at BB13 (ycfaCultJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ycfaCultSignal > 0) {
    pfo3               = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer3         = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedYCFA    = mix ycfaEmulsion with pfo3 for 1m
    extractedDNA_YCFA  = mix demulsifiedYCFA with dnaBuffer3 for 1m

    ycfaSeqSignal      = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_YCFA for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_YCFA
    dispose ycfaSeqSignal
} else {
    drain ycfaEmulsion
}

dispose ycfaCultSignal

// ============================================================
// BB13: ycfaCultJoin
// All rich media cultivation arms complete.
// Control falls into antibiotic resistance screening arm.
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2: ANTIBIOTIC RESISTANCE SCREENING IN DROPLETS
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 1: Ampicillin resistance screening.
//   BHIS medium supplemented with ampicillin at 100 ug/mL.
//   Concentration chosen to be commensurate with commercially
//   available antibiotic selection plates (Boente et al. 2010).
//   Same fecal cell suspension; same Poisson loading (200x
//   dilution); same droplet volume range (65-115 pL).
//   Cultured for 1 day (1440 min) inside the anaerobic chamber.
//   After incubation: optical density-based sorting removes
//   empty droplets (dead/nonviable cells) so that only droplets
//   with a grown colony contribute to sequencing reads.
//   Plate control: stool diluted 10000x; plated on BHIS +
//   ampicillin; cultured 3 days; DNA from plate scraping.
//   Result: 21 total unique resistant organisms detected only
//   in droplets across all three antibiotics.
//   Ampicillin droplets recovered known Bacteroides spp. and
//   Parabacteroides spp. resistance (Boente et al. 2010) and
//   revealed novel Pseudomonas spp. and Shewanella spp.
//   resistance undetected on plates.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ampCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
ampMedium    = dispense 1 units of Ampicillin_BHIS
ampOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

ampPreEmulsion  = mix ampCells with ampMedium for 5s
ampEmulsion     = mix ampPreEmulsion with ampOil for 5s

// 1 day incubation = 1440 min.
heat ampEmulsion at 37c for 1440m

// Sort to remove dead/nonviable droplets (OD < 0.3).
// Only colony-containing droplets enter the sequencing step.
ampResistSignal = detect waveletODSorting on ampEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB14 / BB15: Ampicillin screen QC gate
// Pass (BB14): ampResistSignal > 0 -> resistant colonies
//              detected and sorted; extract DNA, sequence.
// Fail (BB15): ampResistSignal <= 0 -> no viable colonies
//              in ampicillin droplets; drain.
// Both converge at BB16 (ampScreenJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ampResistSignal > 0) {
    pfo4               = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer4         = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedAMP     = mix ampEmulsion with pfo4 for 1m
    extractedDNA_AMP   = mix demulsifiedAMP with dnaBuffer4 for 1m

    ampSeqSignal       = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_AMP for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_AMP
    dispose ampSeqSignal
} else {
    drain ampEmulsion
}

dispose ampResistSignal

// ============================================================
// BB16: ampScreenJoin
// Ampicillin screen complete. Control falls into ciprofloxacin arm.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 2: Ciprofloxacin resistance screening.
//   BHIS medium supplemented with ciprofloxacin at 5 ug/mL.
//   Fluoroquinolone class antibiotic; concentration commensurate
//   with commercially available selection plates.
//   Expected resistors: Enterococcus spp. and Enterobacteriaceae
//   (Hooper 2002; Paterson 2006). Gram-positive bacteria show
//   reduced susceptibility (Poole 2000).
//   Droplet screening also reveals Bacteroides spp. and
//   Parabacteroides spp. fluoroquinolone resistance
//   (Snydman et al. 2017) undetected on plates.
//   Plate control: 4 Clostridium spp. showed higher growth on
//   plates than droplets (only 5 organisms total showed plate
//   preference across all 3 antibiotics).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ciproCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
ciproMedium    = dispense 1 units of Ciprofloxacin_BHIS
ciproOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

ciproPreEmulsion  = mix ciproCells with ciproMedium for 5s
ciproEmulsion     = mix ciproPreEmulsion with ciproOil for 5s

heat ciproEmulsion at 37c for 1440m

ciproResistSignal = detect waveletODSorting on ciproEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB17 / BB18: Ciprofloxacin screen QC gate
// Pass (BB17): ciproResistSignal > 0 -> resistant colonies
//              detected and sorted; extract DNA, sequence.
// Fail (BB18): ciproResistSignal <= 0 -> no viable colonies;
//              drain.
// Both converge at BB19 (ciproScreenJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ciproResistSignal > 0) {
    pfo5               = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer5         = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedCIPRO   = mix ciproEmulsion with pfo5 for 1m
    extractedDNA_CIPRO = mix demulsifiedCIPRO with dnaBuffer5 for 1m

    ciproSeqSignal     = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_CIPRO for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_CIPRO
    dispose ciproSeqSignal
} else {
    drain ciproEmulsion
}

dispose ciproResistSignal

// ============================================================
// BB19: ciproScreenJoin
// Ciprofloxacin screen complete. Control falls into vancomycin arm.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 3: Vancomycin resistance screening.
//   BHIS medium supplemented with vancomycin at 10 ug/mL.
//   Concentration commensurate with commercially available
//   selection plates.
//   Expected resistors: Enterobacteriaceae gen. spp. (intrinsic
//   resistance; Citron et al. 2012).
//   Droplet screening additionally revealed Pseudomonas spp.
//   and Shewanella spp. (Shewanella is a known progenitor of
//   antibiotic resistance genes in humans; Yousfi et al. 2017)
//   resistant to vancomycin -- organisms undetected on plates.
//   These 21 unique droplet-only resistant organisms represent
//   a significant extension of the plate-based assessment.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

vancoCells     = dispense 1 units of FecalCellSuspension
vancoMedium    = dispense 1 units of Vancomycin_BHIS
vancoOil       = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_SurfactantOil

vancoPreEmulsion  = mix vancoCells with vancoMedium for 5s
vancoEmulsion     = mix vancoPreEmulsion with vancoOil for 5s

heat vancoEmulsion at 37c for 1440m

vancoResistSignal = detect waveletODSorting on vancoEmulsion for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB20 / BB21: Vancomycin screen QC gate
// Pass (BB20): vancoResistSignal > 0 -> resistant colonies
//              detected and sorted; extract DNA, sequence.
// Fail (BB21): vancoResistSignal <= 0 -> no viable colonies;
//              drain.
// Both converge at BB22 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (vancoResistSignal > 0) {
    pfo6               = dispense 1 units of PFO_DemulsificationAgent
    dnaBuffer6         = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionBuffer
    demulsifiedVANCO   = mix vancoEmulsion with pfo6 for 1m
    extractedDNA_VANCO = mix demulsifiedVANCO with dnaBuffer6 for 1m

    vancoSeqSignal     = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on extractedDNA_VANCO for 30s
    dispose extractedDNA_VANCO
    dispose vancoSeqSignal
} else {
    drain vancoEmulsion
}

dispose vancoResistSignal

// ============================================================
// BB22: finalCleanup (terminal)
// All protocol arms complete. No further instructions.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
